An algorithm's efficiency isn't measured in seconds—it's measured in growth rate.
Time Complexity quantifies how execution time increases as input size ($n$) grows, while Space Complexity measures additional memory consumed.
Big O Notation describes the worst-case upper bound of an algorithm's resource requirements.
